    "feature": {
      "name": "Surveyor's Standing",
      "desc": [
        "You have drawn maps that other people have staked money and lives on, and those who rely on maps know the worth of the hand that made them. Officials, caravan masters, guild clerks and expedition leaders are willing to hear you out, and you can usually arrange a short meeting with one of them by offering to check or improve their charts of a region.",
        "When you spend a day studying the maps, survey notes or landmarks of a place, you can sketch a map of it that is accurate about distances and the layout of roads, rivers and settlements. Anyone who holds that sketch can use it to find their way through the area you mapped."
      ]
    },
    "personality_traits": {
